  "body": "The page had grown three sections in the order they were *built*, not the order you need them. This reorders it, regroups the settings, and replaces the worst control on the page.\n\n## Structure, top to bottom\n\n| | |\n| --- | --- |\n| **1. Connection** | The one-click panel that writes `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` + `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` — **back at the top**. It's what most people came for and it was third. |\n| **2. No setup needed** | Launcher commands for **every** agent, not just Claude Code: `mcc-claude`, `mcc-claude --discover-models`, `mcc-codex`, `mcc-pi`, `mcc-claude-old` — each with a copy button, plus one line noting the `fcc-*` spellings still work. |\n| **3. All settings** | Unchanged in behaviour, regrouped. |\n\nThe old two-card \"choose how you connect\" block is gone — it said *\"use the Configure panel below\"* and duplicated what the panel already said.\n\n## Nine groups instead of sixteen categories\n\nNamed for **what you're configuring**: Model and reasoning · Context and cost · Permissions and safety · Tools · Agents, skills, and automation · MCP · Connection and providers · Interface · Privacy, telemetry, and updates.\n\nThe previous grouping was the docs' own mechanical categories — several held one or two rows while *every* `settings.json` key fell into a single \"settings\" bucket. The group is computed in the generator and carried in the catalog, so the page and `docs/CLAUDE-CODE-CONFIG.md` can't disagree about where a setting lives.\n\n## Array settings are lists now, not JSON\n\nEach entry is a row with a remove button plus an add field — so the most common edit in the file, **adding one permission rule**, stops being an exercise in matching brackets.\n\nFor `permissions.allow` / `ask` / `deny` that add field is a **rule builder**: tool dropdown (Bash, PowerShell, Read, Edit, WebFetch, Agent, Cd, WebSearch, `mcp__server`), a specifier field with a per-tool placeholder and hint, and a live preview of the rule it will add.\n\n## Accessibility (from the ui-ux-pro-max checklist)\n\n- Every control now has a real **`<label for>`** carrying the setting name — previously styled text with nothing associating it. List and rule editors have no single control to point at, so those are `role=\"group\"` + `aria-labelledby`; a label aimed at a nonexistent id reads as labelled and isn't.\n- JSON errors appear **next to the field** with `role=\"alert\"` and `aria-invalid`, not only as a toast at the top.\n\n## Bugs found by driving the page\n\n- **A bulk edit had injected `input.id = controlId` into `inputForField()`** — the *generic* field renderer shared by **Model Config, Limits and Messaging**, where no such variable exists. Every boolean toggle on those three pages would have thrown. Caught by the page reporting `controlId is not defined`; fix verified by counting rendered checkboxes on all three (2, 11, 1).\n- The toggle wrapped its checkbox in a second `<label>`, so **41 rows were unlabelled**.\n- The `group` field was computed but never carried through `CatalogEntry`, so **all 101 rows rendered in one section**.\n- Copy buttons were wired once at startup, when the view is hidden.\n- Long commands ran **underneath** the absolutely-positioned copy button.\n- Descriptions showed raw markdown (`**Default**:`, backslash-escaped underscores).\n- One more undefined-token usage fixed — the stylesheet now has **none**. Dead `.claude-connect-*` rules removed with the markup that used them.\n\n## Verification\n\nReal browser, live server, throwaway home port 8175 (**WSL :8082 never touched**, still 200):\n\n- Nine groups with sensible counts; 101 rows default.\n- All five launcher rows have a working copy button, no text under it.\n- **Zero broken labels**, checked by resolving every label target. Clicking a setting name toggles its checkbox.\n- Rule builder: picked WebFetch, typed `domain:evil.example.com`, preview read `WebFetch(domain:evil.example.com)` with the hostname hint. Adding put it in the list, removing `Bash(rm *)` took it out, the diff showed the whole before/after array, and **on disk** the deny list held exactly the two intended rules with the credential untouched.\n- Model Config / Limits / Messaging still render their boolean fields.\n- No console errors.\n- 5 new grouping contract tests, including one that **fails if any group ever swallows more than a third of the catalog**. Full suite **3784 passed**, same 14 environment-baseline failures.\n\nMINOR bump **5.9.0 → 5.10.0**.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TWCKNkSxNEfus8GfcqXnQD\n",
