    "message": "feat(admin): restructure the Configure Claude Code page around what you configure\n\nThe page had grown three sections in the order they were built rather than the\norder you need them: a \"choose how you connect\" explainer, then the panel that\nactually connects you, then the settings editor grouped by the docs' own\nsixteen mechanical categories. This reorders and regroups it, and replaces the\nworst control on the page.\n\nStructure, top to bottom:\n\n1. Connection -- the one-click panel that writes ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and\n   ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, back at the top where it belongs. It is what most\n   people came for and it was third.\n2. No setup needed -- the launcher commands, now covering every agent rather\n   than only Claude Code: mcc-claude, mcc-claude --discover-models, mcc-codex,\n   mcc-pi, mcc-claude-old, each with a copy button, plus one line noting the\n   fcc-* spellings still work. The old two-card layout said \"use the Configure\n   panel below\" and duplicated what the panel already said.\n3. All Claude Code settings -- unchanged in behaviour, regrouped.\n\nGrouping is now nine sections named for what you are configuring (Model and\nreasoning, Context and cost, Permissions and safety, Tools, Agents/skills/\nautomation, MCP, Connection and providers, Interface, Privacy/telemetry/\nupdates) instead of sixteen mechanical categories, several of which held one or\ntwo rows while every settings.json key fell into a single \"settings\" bucket.\nThe group is computed in the generator and carried in the catalog, so the page\nand docs/CLAUDE-CODE-CONFIG.md cannot disagree about where a setting lives.\n\nArray settings are no longer a JSON textarea. Each entry is a row with a remove\nbutton, and there is an add field -- so the most common edit in the file,\nadding one permission rule, stops being an exercise in matching brackets. For\npermissions.allow/ask/deny that add field is a rule builder: a tool dropdown\n(Bash, PowerShell, Read, Edit, WebFetch, Agent, Cd, WebSearch, mcp__server),\na specifier field with a per-tool placeholder and hint, and a live preview of\nthe rule it will add.\n\nAccessibility, from the ui-ux-pro-max checklist:\n- Every control now has a real <label for> carrying the setting name, which was\n  previously styled text with nothing associating it. List and rule editors\n  have no single control to point at, so those are role=\"group\" with\n  aria-labelledby instead -- a label aimed at an id that does not exist reads\n  as labelled and is not.\n- JSON validation errors now appear next to the field with role=\"alert\" and\n  aria-invalid, not only as a toast at the top of the page.\n\nBugs fixed along the way, all found by driving the page:\n\n- A bulk edit had injected `input.id = controlId` into inputForField(), the\n  GENERIC field renderer shared by Model Config, Limits and Messaging, where no\n  such variable exists. Every boolean toggle on those three pages would have\n  thrown. Caught by the page reporting \"controlId is not defined\"; the fix is\n  verified by counting rendered checkboxes on all three views (2, 11, 1).\n- The toggle control wrapped its checkbox in a second <label>, so the row label\n  had no id to target and 41 rows were unlabelled.\n- The group field was computed but never carried through CatalogEntry, so all\n  101 default rows rendered in one section.\n- Copy buttons were wired once at startup, when the view is hidden; they are\n  now wired when the view opens too.\n- Long commands ran underneath the absolutely-positioned copy button.\n- Descriptions showed raw markdown: **Default**: and backslash-escaped\n  underscores are stripped along with links and backticks.\n- One more undefined-token usage (var(--input-bg, var(--surface))) fixed, so\n  the stylesheet now has none. The dead .claude-connect-* rules are removed\n  with the markup that used them.\n\nVerification, real browser against a live server on a throwaway home (port\n8175, WSL :8082 never touched, still answering 200):\n- Nine groups render with sensible counts; 101 rows in the default view.\n- All five launcher rows have a working copy button and no text runs under it.\n- Zero rows with a broken label, checked by resolving every label target.\n  Clicking a setting name toggles its checkbox.\n- Rule builder: picked WebFetch, typed domain:evil.example.com, preview read\n  WebFetch(domain:evil.example.com) with the hostname hint; adding put it in\n  the list, removing Bash(rm *) took it out, and the diff showed the whole\n  before/after array. On disk afterwards the deny list held exactly the two\n  intended rules and the credential was untouched.\n- Model Config, Limits and Messaging still render their boolean fields.\n- No console errors.\n- 5 new grouping contract tests, including one that fails if any group ever\n  swallows more than a third of the catalog. Full suite 3784 passed with the\n  same 14 environment-baseline failures as an untouched worktree.\n\nMINOR bump 5.9.0 -> 5.10.0.",
